            <div xml:id="d468-a4">

                <pb facs="0840" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg740"/>

                <p rendition="#center">(Copy, No. 2.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Republic, Department of War and Marine,
                        Section</hi> 1.</p>
                <p>General Abraham Plata telegraphs me the following from Morella:</p>
                <p>“To-day, the colonel of the second corps of auxiliaries communicated to me from
                    Maravatio the following: ‘Captain Ocanas reports from Zitácuaro a mutiny in
                    Anganqueo. There were five persons killed, I have ordered forces to that point.
                    I go with 50 cavalry.’</p>
                <p>“I asked information and the major of the same corps replied to me with the
                    following: ‘The colonel has marched with 55 men. The detachment from Zitácuaro
                    has marched. A. servant of the house of Murga, who left Anganqueo this morning,
                    reports that the miners mutinied against the company on account of the killing
                    of an operative, <pb facs="0841" n="741" xml:id="pg741"/> and burnt a house, and
                    that four foreigners were killed. Nothing unusual on this line.’”</p>
                <p>And I transcribe it to you for your information.</p>
                <p>Liberty in the Constitution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Mexico</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1880-03-16">March 16, 1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MONTESINOS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of Foreign Affairs</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Present.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
